// Cross-track contracts fixed up front so parallel tracks can build against them.
const CONTRACTS = [
  "CROSS-TRACK CONTRACTS (fixed; implement your side exactly, report any deviation):",
  "C1 Session cookies. POST /api/v1/auth/login, /auth/refresh, /auth/logout (staff) and /api/v1/portal/auth/login, /portal/auth/refresh, /portal/auth/logout: when the request carries header 'X-KKT-Session: cookie', the API sets the refresh token as cookie kkt_rt (staff, Path=/api/v1/auth) or kkt_prt (portal, Path=/api/v1/portal/auth) with HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Secure unless NODE_ENV is development/test, Max-Age = remaining absolute lifetime, and leaves refresh_token out of the JSON body (the contract field becomes optional). Refresh reads the cookie when the body has no refresh_token, and cookie-based refresh/logout require the X-KKT-Session: cookie header (CSRF guard). Logout clears the cookie. Body mode stays for native apps and API clients. A refresh-token family has an absolute lifetime REFRESH_ABSOLUTE_TTL_DAYS (default 30): rotation never extends it; past it refresh answers 401 SESSION_EXPIRED. CORS for the ERP/portal origins allows credentials.",
  "C2 Client error reporting. POST /api/v1/client-errors, no auth required (a bearer token is used for attribution when present), body {app: 'erp'|'portal'|'web', message (<= 2 KB), stack? (<= 8 KB), url?, release?, user_agent?, extra? (object)}, 16 KB body limit, per-IP rate limited, answers 202 {accepted: true}; logged at warn with pino and counted in metric kkt_client_errors_total{app}. Never stores PII beyond what the client sends; strips query strings from url.",
  "C3 Website server-to-API. Next.js server-side fetches send 'x-kkt-internal-token: <INTERNAL_API_TOKEN>' and 'x-kkt-client-ip: <visitor ip>'. With a valid token (constant-time compare) the API applies public rate limits per the forwarded client IP instead of the Next server IP; without a valid token both headers are ignored. Public rate limits use separate buckets per route group (catalog reads, forms, brochure, visits).",
  "C4 Tenant resolution. apps/api/src/lib/tenant.ts exports resolveCompanyId(app, req): (1) the authenticated principal's company; (2) header 'x-kkt-company: <company slug>'; (3) the request Host matched against companies.hosts; (4) the only company when exactly one exists; otherwise 400 COMPANY_REQUIRED. Staff and portal login bodies accept optional 'company' (slug). The website sends x-kkt-company from env KKT_COMPANY_SLUG when set.",
  "C5 Public caching. A route opts in with Fastify route config { cachePolicy: { public: true, sMaxAge: <s>, staleWhileRevalidate: <s> } }; the platform hook then sets Cache-Control 'public, s-maxage=…, stale-while-revalidate=…', a strong ETag over the body and answers 304 to a matching If-None-Match. Without cachePolicy responses stay no-store. Authenticated responses are always no-store.",
  "C6 Versions. Versioned resources return a numeric 'version' field; single-resource GETs and writes set ETag \"v<version>\". Writes accept If-Match \"v<version>\" or the legacy forms version.ts already accepts, or body 'expected_version'. Missing where required: 428 VERSION_REQUIRED; stale: 409 VERSION_CONFLICT with details.current_version.",
  "C7 Ledger history. The booking ledger is append-only and versioned by epoch: GET /api/v1/bookings/:id/ledger keeps its shape for the current epoch and adds 'epoch'; ?epoch=n reads an older epoch; GET /api/v1/bookings/:id/ledger/rebuilds lists rebuilds {from_epoch, to_epoch, reason, actor, at, summary}. The ledger response carries a server-computed 'summary' {cash_due_paise, account_due_paise, total_due_paise, other_charges_due_paise, cash_paid_paise, account_paid_paise} that clients must use instead of the last row of a page.",
  "C8 Worker health. The worker serves GET /health on WORKER_HEALTH_PORT (default 9465): 200 {status:'ok', redis, queues, last_heartbeat_at} or 503; it writes a heartbeat to Redis every 15 s and exports kkt_worker_heartbeat_timestamp_seconds. Drain timeout WORKER_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_MS (default 120000 for the critical queue; heavy jobs checkpoint and resume).",
  "C9 Secrets. JWT_SIGNING_KEYS = comma list of '<kid>:<base64 PKCS8 DER Ed25519 private key>' (first is active; all are published in JWKS); LINK_SIGNING_KEYS and HASH_KEYS = comma lists of '<kid>:<secret>' (first active; older ones verify/lookup only). Each has a _FILE variant. Outside production they may be derived from JWT_SECRET/HASH_KEY as today; in production the explicit rings are required and placeholder values are rejected at boot.",
].join("\n");

